00:05:58.332 --> 00:06:00.979
the (bleep) stuff going on in our lives.

00:06:00.979 --> 00:06:03.522
I find group therapy really powerful

00:06:03.522 --> 00:06:05.509
because if it's just one on one,

00:06:05.509 --> 00:06:06.677
I can say I just disagree with you,

00:06:06.677 --> 00:06:08.009
but when four or five people are saying,

00:06:08.009 --> 00:06:09.765
"Hey dude, no you're really
coming off like that,"

00:06:09.765 --> 00:06:12.520
or you're really having this
problem in your relationship

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:14.310
and maybe need to look at it,
and five people are saying it

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:16.930
like it's pretty hard to dismiss them.

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:18.518
I know a lot of my friends
have written really, really

00:06:18.518 --> 00:06:21.199
successful books, and even I
wrote a book called "The Game,"

00:06:21.199 --> 00:06:22.784
which has probably sold like

00:06:22.784 --> 00:06:26.731
millions of copies, and
really when I wrote it,

00:06:26.731 --> 00:06:28.134
I thought nobody would read it.

00:06:28.134 --> 00:06:29.733
I thought nobody would
read it, but I thought,

00:06:29.733 --> 00:06:32.903
this story's so crazy I just
have to tell this story.

00:06:32.903 --> 00:06:34.873
So these things that seem
you can spend all your time

00:06:34.873 --> 00:06:36.859
trying to engineer the perfect thing,

00:06:36.859 --> 00:06:38.959
and the truth is, we have no control.

00:06:38.959 --> 00:06:40.543
